 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,1),(-2,3),(-1,-5).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302255 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302256 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302257 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302258 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1000 #edb/ref 17592186302259 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1041 "selection" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1104 #edb/ref 17592186302258 13194139534665 true] [17592186302254 1110 #uuid "108ada0e-2296-5b6c-9dff-d68f0bc0682b" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302255 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534665 true] [17592186302255 1111 #uuid "698904b5-8def-56f9-808f-1f86e923f280" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302256 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534665 true] [17592186302256 1111 #uuid "fe1156bd-ba34-57e6-82d4-076adca071a5" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302257 1034 "III only" 13194139534665 true] [17592186302257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534665 true] [17592186302257 1111 #uuid "efe11742-d61d-5bd2-a765-ee8df2c69bef" 13194139534665 